questions.solution:
Phenol is a weak acid. It reacts with $\mathrm{NaOH}$ to produce salt.

\begin{array}{r}
\mathrm{C}_{6} \mathrm{H}_{5} \mathrm{OH}+\mathrm{NaOH} \longrightarrow \\
\qquad \begin{aligned}
\mathrm{C}_{6} \mathrm{H}_{5} \mathrm{ONa} \\
\text { sodium phenoxide }
\end{aligned}+\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}
\end{array}$
But it is not sufficiently acidic to evolve $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ from NaHCO _{3}$ solution.

